# Keep text files at LF in every checkout.
#
# The adapter source-contract tests in `crates/guide-adapter/tests/lua_source.rs`
# read the Lua/JSON sources byte for byte and match multi-line snippets. The
# committed blobs are already LF, but a Windows checkout with the common
# `core.autocrlf=true` setting rewrites them to CRLF, which makes those snippet
# matches fail even though nothing changed. Pinning `eol=lf` keeps the working
# tree identical to what CI sees.
*.rs text eol=lf
*.lua text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.jsonl text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.txt text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=lf
*.cpp text eol=lf
*.hpp text eol=lf
*.h text eol=lf
*.def text eol=lf

# `Cargo.toml` is the one text file still *stored* with CRLF. Leave it alone
# here so this change stays line-ending-free; renormalize it in its own commit
# before adding `*.toml text eol=lf` to the list above.
Cargo.toml -text
